From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:41:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: connector: pcie-m2-e-connector: Add
 local-bd-address

The Bluetooth function of an M.2 Key E card attached over UART has no
devicetree node of its own: the power sequencing driver creates one at
runtime when the card appears on PCIe. Boot firmware that assigns the
platform's Bluetooth address therefore has no node to put it in.

Allow the connector node to carry that address as local-bd-address, in
the format used by Bluetooth controller nodes (least significant byte
first).

TODO: this property has not been reviewed upstream. Manivannan
Sadhasivam's posted rework of M.2 Bluetooth instantiation onto the
auxiliary bus removes the runtime node, so how the address reaches the
Bluetooth driver needs to be agreed there.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 .../bindings/connector/pcie-m2-e-connector.yaml          | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/connector/pcie-m2-e-connector.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/connector/pcie-m2-e-connector.yaml
index f7859aa9b63..7492c0e045e 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/connector/pcie-m2-e-connector.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/connector/pcie-m2-e-connector.yaml
@@ -72,6 +72,15 @@ properties:
       M.2 Specification r4.0, sec 3.1.7 for more details.
     maxItems: 1
 
+  local-bd-address:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint8-array
+    minItems: 6
+    maxItems: 6
+    description: BD address assigned to the Bluetooth function of the fitted
+      card, typically filled in by the boot firmware from the platform's
+      provisioning data. Formatted with least significant byte first, as for
+      Bluetooth controller nodes.
+
   vendor-porta-gpios:
     description: GPIO for the first vendor specific signal (VENDOR_PORTA). This
       signal's functionality is defined by the card manufacturer and may be
